  "version": "other",
  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id)\n(section) 7-13-710(A) new item (6), SECTION 1\n(quote) South Carolina resident concealed weapon permit issued pursuant to Article 4, Chapter 31, Title 23.\n(b_no_id_remedy) not stated.\n(c_mail_ballot_id) not stated.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship) not stated.\n(e_other_rule) not stated.\n(other) SECTION 2: takes effect on the Governor's approval. Nothing else.\n(other) version: 2014-12-11_Introduced: adds a sixth item (SC resident concealed weapon permit) to the 7-13-710(A) ID list; no other change to slots a-d.\n(other) version: 2016-04-13_Comm-Sub: House Judiciary 'favorable' report with no amendment; operative text word-for-word identical to the introduced version.\n(other) note: The saved text shows the new item (6) without {{new: }} markers (only the legend lines carry them); it is a bill 'amending by adding' so the whole item is new. It does not reprint the rest of the ID list; the list it adds to is the Act 27 of 2011 list (driver's licence, DMV photo ID, passport, military photo ID, photo voter registration card). Passed the House on second and third reading, then went to Senate Judiciary and stopped (last action 2016-04-28).",
